      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The end point in a titration of a 50.00-mL sample of aqueous HCl was reached by addition of 35.23 mL of 0.250 M NaOH titrant. The titration reaction is:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "fcb77121e8db449b851ef52b8d2db6b9",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "57zhellxre81s7s",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "4ua3xdpmj166dlm",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{HCl}(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm{NaOH}(aq)\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\mathrm{NaCl}(aq)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "What is the molarity of the HCl?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ac160bb90abd4a7aa596ea44c9ecc857",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "As for all reaction stoichiometry calculations, the key issue is the relation between the molar amounts of the chemical species of interest as depicted in the balanced chemical equation. The approach outlined previously is followed with additional considerations required, since the amounts of reactants provided and requested are expressed as solution concentrations."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "b548d4a2437c480a8e6a1e9427bfa93f",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "alt": "Convert volume of NaOH to moles of NaOH using the molar concentration. Convert moles of NaOH to moles of HCl using the stoichiometric factor. Convert moles of HCl to concentration of HCl using the solution volume.",
                "caption": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": " ",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "e2d36347f2b442e2874650d79496b95d",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "nu6spcpn6nf7ygy",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "e52557e6d3634918ad969d705ce05ca7",
                "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/72/72b3ccd4104d15394011f475f9a072be/convert.png",
                "style": "inline",
                "type": "img",
                "vertical-align": "middle"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The molar amount of HCl is calculated to be:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "bf64ef4b23734821a2c74e529e8968df",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "3hsivkoyvs1rgcd",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "cm2mka3sw8pbpck",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\require{cancel}35.23\\;\\cancel{\\mathrm{mL}\\;\\mathrm{NaOH}}\\;\\times\\frac{1\\cancel{\\;\\mathrm L\\;\\mathrm{NaOH}}}{1000\\;\\cancel{\\mathrm{mL}\\;\\mathrm{NaOH}\\;}}\\;\\times\\;\\frac{0.250\\;\\cancel{\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm{NaOH}}}{1\\;\\cancel{\\mathrm L\\;\\mathrm{NaOH}}}\\;\\times\\;\\frac{1\\;\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm{HCl}}{1\\;\\cancel{\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm{NaOH}}}\\;=\\;8.81\\times10^{-3\\;}\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm{HCl}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Using the provided volume of HCl solution and the definition of molarity, the HCl concentration is:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "c25d08e3f21c4a119d3fc172c571127f",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "y70n3hxhdfpo7ua",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "h09e6wb7hd1nlka",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\require{cancel}\\begin{array}{l}M=\\frac{\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm{HCl}}{\\mathrm L\\;\\mathrm{solution}}\\\\M=\\frac{8.81\\times10^{-3}\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm{HCl}}{50.00\\;\\mathrm{mL}\\times{\\displaystyle\\frac{1\\;\\mathrm L}{1000\\;\\mathrm{mL}}}}\\\\M=0.176\\;\\mathrm M\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3803363181",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
